{"html":"<p>Loading data from an API takes time: 50 milliseconds, or 5 seconds on a bad network. JavaScript runs on one thread, so if it simply waited, the whole page would freeze. Instead, slow operations return a <strong>promise</strong>, and your code continues when the result is ready.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-promise-is\">What a Promise Is</h2>\n<p>A promise is an object that stands for a value that will arrive <strong>later</strong>. It&#39;s in one of three states:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>pending:</strong> still waiting,</li>\n<li><strong>fulfilled:</strong> done, with a value,</li>\n<li><strong>rejected:</strong> failed, with an error.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>fetch</code>, which loads data over HTTP, returns a promise. So do most browser and Node APIs that take time.</p>\n<h2 id=\"then-and-catch\">then and catch</h2>\n<p>The classic way to use a result is to register a callback:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"1. before\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">wait</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"data\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">then</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">value</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"3. got\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, value));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"2. after\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>The output is &quot;1. before&quot;, &quot;2. after&quot;, then &quot;3. got data&quot;: the code after the call runs <strong>first</strong>, and the callback runs once the promise is fulfilled. <code>catch</code> handles a rejection, and both return new promises, so they chain.</p>\n<h2 id=\"async-and-await\">async and await</h2>\n<p><code>await</code> pauses an <code>async</code> function until a promise settles, so asynchronous code reads like normal code:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">async</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> load</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> user</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> await</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> getUser</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> orders</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> await</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> getOrders</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(user.id);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> { user, orders };</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Two rules:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>await</code> only works inside an <code>async</code> function (or at the top of a module).</li>\n<li>An <code>async</code> function <strong>always returns a promise</strong>, even if you <code>return 42</code>. The caller has to <code>await</code> it too.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>While <code>load</code> waits, the page stays responsive: other code, clicks and rendering keep running. The <a href=\"/blog/essentials/javascript-event-loop-explained/\">event loop article</a> shows how.</p>\n<h2 id=\"handling-errors\">Handling Errors</h2>\n<p>A rejected promise makes <code>await</code> <strong>throw</strong>, so you use the familiar <code>try</code> and <code>catch</code>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">async</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> safeLoad</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  try</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> await</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> loadData</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">    show</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(data);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  } </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">catch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (error) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Failed:\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, error.message);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  } </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">finally</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">    hideSpinner</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h3 id=\"fetch-doesn-t-reject-on-http-errors\">fetch Doesn&#39;t Reject on HTTP Errors</h3>\n<p>A classic surprise: <code>fetch</code> only rejects when the network fails. A <strong>404 or 500 is a successful promise</strong>. Check <code>response.ok</code> yourself:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">async</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> getUser</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">id</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> response</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> await</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fetch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">`/api/users/${</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">id</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">}`</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">!</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">response.ok) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    throw</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Error</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">`HTTP ${</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">response</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">status</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">}`</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> response.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">json</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// also returns a promise</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"sequential-vs-parallel\">Sequential vs Parallel</h2>\n<p>Each <code>await</code> waits before the next line starts. Two independent 50 ms calls in a row take 100 ms:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> a</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> await</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> getA</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 50 ms</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> b</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> await</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> getB</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// then 50 ms more</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Start them together with <code>Promise.all</code>, and it takes about 50 ms:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">a</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">b</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> await</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Promise</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">all</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">([</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getA</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(), </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getB</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">()]);</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Only run in sequence when the second call needs the first one&#39;s result.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-promise-helpers\">The Promise Helpers</h3>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Helper</th>\n<th>Resolves when…</th>\n<th>Rejects when…</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Promise.all</code></td>\n<td>All succeed, with all the values</td>\n<td>Any one fails</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Promise.allSettled</code></td>\n<td>All finish, with each status</td>\n<td>Never</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Promise.race</code></td>\n<td>The first to finish succeeds</td>\n<td>The first to finish fails</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Promise.any</code></td>\n<td>The first one succeeds</td>\n<td>All of them fail</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p><code>allSettled</code> is useful for dashboards: show what loaded, and an error only for the widget that failed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"promises-and-the-event-loop\">Promises and the Event Loop</h2>\n<p>Promise callbacks run before timers, even a 0 ms timer:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setTimeout</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"timeout\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">Promise</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">resolve</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">then</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"microtask\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"sync\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// sync, microtask, timeout</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Synchronous code runs first, then promise callbacks (microtasks), then timers.</p>\n<h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common Mistakes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Forgetting <code>await</code>:</strong> <code>const user = getUser();</code> gives a pending promise, not a user. TypeScript catches many of these.</li>\n<li><strong><code>await</code> in a loop for independent work:</strong> <code>for (const id of ids) await load(id)</code> runs one at a time. Use <code>Promise.all(ids.map(load))</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Unhandled rejections:</strong> a promise that fails with no <code>catch</code> logs an error and can crash Node. Always handle errors at some level.</li>\n<li><strong>Not checking <code>response.ok</code></strong> after <code>fetch</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>forEach</code> with async callbacks:</strong> <code>forEach</code> doesn&#39;t wait for them. Use <code>for...of</code> with <code>await</code>, or <code>Promise.all</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>A promise stands for a future value: pending, then fulfilled or rejected.</li>\n<li><code>await</code> pauses an <code>async</code> function until the promise settles; the page stays responsive meanwhile.</li>\n<li>Use <code>try</code> / <code>catch</code> around <code>await</code>, and check <code>response.ok</code>, because <code>fetch</code> doesn&#39;t reject on 404 or 500.</li>\n<li>Run independent requests in parallel with <code>Promise.all</code>; use <code>allSettled</code> when partial results are fine.</li>\n<li>Promise callbacks run before timers, after the current synchronous code.</li>\n</ol>\n"}